A(('p', '3.8 What the stories leave unsaid. Neither story says who the one who asks is, who the one who answers is, or what is asked beyond the loaves and the avenging. Neither says what happens after the giving. The word for the one who gives way is “friend” in the first and “judge” in the second, and the text does not say that the two are alike in anything else. Each account is read as it stands.'))

