A(('p', '4.1 What Jesus says after the friend. After the story Jesus says: “I say unto you, Though he will not rise and give him, because he is his friend, yet because of his importunity he will rise and give him as many as he needeth” (Luke 11:8). He goes on: “And I say unto you, Ask, and it shall be given you; seek, and ye shall find; knock, and it shall be opened unto you” (11:9), and “For every one that asketh receiveth; and he that seeketh findeth; and to him that knocketh it shall be opened” (11:10). He then asks about a son and a father, and closes, “If ye then, being evil, know how to give good gifts unto your children: how much more shall your heavenly Father give the Holy Spirit to them that ask him?” (11:13). Everything Jesus names in Luke 11:8–13 is in those verses, and the table records it in His words.'))
